CHAPTER X

INSTITUTIONAL FRAMEWORK

Article 79

(1) The Women's Empowerment and Child Protection System is the entire process of organizing women's empowerment and child protection carried out comprehensively, inclusively and integratively starting from the stage of report/complaint handling services, health services, social rehabilitation, repatriation, social reintegration and legal assistance up to repatriation and social reintegration for women and children victims of crime and violence in their social environment.

2. The Women's Empowerment and Child Protection System aims to:a. improve the quality of life of women, children and the quality of families;
b. increase the institutional capacity of women's empowerment and child protection including the development of gender and child data; andc. provide special protection for children from various forms of violence and other discriminatory treatment.
3. The Women's Empowerment and Child Protection System is carried out through:a. providing access for women and children to education, health and other strategic services;
b. encouraging the involvement of women and children in the development process;
