CHAPTER X

INSTITUTIONAL FRAMEWORK

Article 79

(1) The Women's Empowerment and Child Protection System is the entire process of organizing women's empowerment and child protection carried out comprehensively, inclusively and integratively starting from the stage of report/complaint handling services, health services, social rehabilitation, repatriation, social reintegration and legal assistance up to repatriation and social reintegration for women and children victims of crime and violence in their social environment.

2. The Women's Empowerment and Child Protection System aims to:a. improve the quality of life of women, children and the quality of families;
b. increase the institutional capacity of women's empowerment and child protection including the development of gender and child data; andc. provide special protection for children from various forms of violence and other discriminatory treatment.
3. The Women's Empowerment and Child Protection System is carried out through:a. providing access for women and children to education, health and other strategic services;
b. encouraging the involvement of women and children in the development process;
c. providing knowledge, skills, character values, morals and family resilience;

JDIH Kota Singkawang
d. encouraging programs that can increase women's independence in the economic, political, legal, socio-cultural and other strategic fields;
e. establishment, development and strengthening of the capacity of Women and Child Protection institutions including complaint service units for violence against women and children as well as legal aid services;
f. improving the quality of human resources of managers;
g. strengthening the institutional capacity of regional gender and child mainstreaming;
h. strengthening and developing gender and child data systems; and
I. carrying out promotive, preventive, curative and rehabilitative efforts in accordance with Laws and Regulations.
4. In order to achieve comprehensive, inclusive and integrative women's empowerment and child protection in the region, the Regional Government shall establish:a. P2TP2A or similar institutions that have the same functions and roles;
b. regional child protection commission or other similar institutions to support supervision of the implementation of child protection in the region; andc. other institutions according to needs and/or provisions of Laws and Regulations.

